  "modelAssumptions": [
    "Demand is linear: people times a per-person rate times the site's tempo (Spoke B runs at 1.5 for flying operations).",
    "Fuel is consumed whether or not generators run; generators need fuel at the site to produce power.",
    "Fuel from another island arrives only on barge days. Fuel does not fly.",
    "Spoke B can store five days of fuel; it opens with three.",
    "Missing operator or maintenance lines do not cut capacity; they raise the daily chance of equipment going down.",
    "Main Island utilities never fail in this scenario so the lesson stays at Spoke B.",
    "Mission output counts each open site equally, so the spoke weighs as much as the hub.",
    "Third Island is on the host-nation grid, so Spoke C power is not tracked and water does not wait on it.",
    "Spoke C's advance team asked for bottled water only; the island's well plant vendor offers supply with operators and maintenance but needs six days to mobilize."
  ]
}
